# Docker
# You might want to gitignore Docker-related files *within* your service directories
# if you have Dockerfiles, docker-compose.yml, etc., there.  But it's often BEST
# to keep those IN version control.  So, I am NOT including general Docker ignores
# by default here.  Add them if you really don't want them in version control:
# !docker-compose.yml  <-- Example of how to *keep* a file
# Dockerfile*
# .dockerignore

# IDE-Specific (Add more as needed, but .idea/ and .vscode/ are common)
# .idea/ and .vscode are included in the General section at the beginning

